  "pages": [
    {
      "anchor": "casing",
      "type": "blocks/2",
      "header": "Turbine Casing",
      "block1": "nuclearcraft:turbine_glass",
      "block2": "nuclearcraft:turbine_casing",
      "text": "The interior components of the turbine are contained within a rectangular prism. The turbine must have edges consisting of $(thing)Turbine Casing$(), while the walls of the turbine can be $(thing)Turbine Glass$(), Turbine Casing, or both."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "controller",
      "type": "blocks/1",
      "header": "Turbine Controller",
      "block": "nuclearcraft:turbine_controller",
      "text": "Without a controller, the turbine multiblock will not form. Its GUI will show information about the turbine, such as the averages of relevant components' stats."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "port",
      "type": "blocks/1",
      "header": "Turbine Port",
      "block": "nuclearcraft:turbine_port",
      "text": "The Turbine Port is used to transfer fluids and energy into and out of the turbine. It can be configured to input or output fluids and energy. The port can also be used for redstone control and computers."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "coils",
      "type": "blocks/2",
      "block1": "nuclearcraft:turbine_copper_coil,nuclearcraft:turbine_magnesium_coil,nuclearcraft:turbine_silver_coil,nuclearcraft:turbine_gold_coil,nuclearcraft:turbine_beryllium_coil,nuclearcraft:turbine_aluminum_coil",
      "header": "Coils",
      "text": "$(thing)Coils$() are used to convert the rotor's kinetic energy into electricity. All coils have different efficiencies and placement rules."
    },
